def is_prime(n: int) -> bool:
    if n < 2:
        return False
    if n < 4:          # 2, 3
        return True
    if n % 2 == 0:
        return False
    i = 3
    while i * i <= n:
        if n % i == 0:
            return False
        i += 2
    return True
```

Trial division up to `sqrt(n)`, skipping even divisors after handling 2. O(√n) time, O(1) space. Edge cases: `n < 2` → `False`; `2`, `3` → `True`.
